From c5c787fa6a0baf4acc19af44805ba25faf6f4531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:43:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(host-contracts): ACL v0.4.3 with the E2 retirement
 certificate (lifecycle Level 3, v0.13 line)

Main's E2 (lifecycle/level3 3d085806) on the v0.13 line, after E1's v0.4.2:
retireAccountWithSig(account, successor, chainIds, signature) with the same
checks, order, EIP-712 domain ("DecryptionAuthorityLifecycle", "1"), type
hash and ERC-165 id (0x4b9ec076); retireAccount() and the certificate share
_retire(). The function bodies are byte-identical to main's.

Version 0.4.3, reinitializer 8, reinitializeV7() (no new state). The upgrade
matrix moves the v0.4.1 -> v0.4.2 cases onto a v0.4.2 fixture and adds U9
(v0.4.2 -> v0.4.3: E1 state preserved, a certificate works right after).

The Foundry profile turns the optimizer on (800 runs, as this line's Hardhat
production build): unoptimized, the ACL with E1 already exceeded EIP-170.
The ERC-165 fuzz test now excludes every declared id (as main 5cd12ed5): the
fuzzer draws PUSH4 constants from the bytecode and found 0x4b9ec076.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
